               System Monitoring Tools

1. df -h : check disk usage
--> Displays disk space usage of mounted filesystem.
--> -h means human readable (MB,GB)
--> Checking the entire hard disk
--> df -h vs du -sh

2. free -h :
--> Shows RAM memory usage

3. uptime:
-->  displays how long the system has been running since its last boot.

4. lscpu:
--> shows CPU hardware information

5. cat /etc/os-release
--> Displaysnthe linux distribution name, version and other OS details.

6. whoami :
--> displays the username of the user currently executing the command.
 
              